 61FE c  2007Ve05: {+61}Fe isomer populated and aligned following the           
 61FE2c  fragmentation of a 64.6 MeV/nucleon {+64}Ni beam from GANIL accelerator
 61FE3c  impinging on a 94.1 mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be target. Fully stripped fragments  
 61FE4c  selected by the LISE fragment separator and implanted in a Cd single   
 61FE5c  crystal. Measured spectroscopic quadrupole moment of the 9/2+ isomer   
 61FE6c  by ion-implantation TDPAD method and four Ge detectors at angles of    
 61FE7c  -24|', -114|', 145|' and 66|' relative to the secondary beam.          
 61FE c  2004Ma80: E=54.7 MeV/nucleon {+64}Ni beam from GANIL accelerator.      
 61FE2c  Fragmentation process used to produce {+61}Fe nuclei which were        
 61FE3c  separated using the LISE fragment separator and implanted in a Cu      
 61FE4c  host. Measured half-life and g factor of the 9/2+ isomer by            
 61FE5c  time-dependent perturbed angular distribution TDPAD method and four    
 61FE6c  Ge detectors at angles -45|', -135|', 45|', 135|' relative to          
 61FE7c  the secondary beam.                                                    
 61FE c  1998Gr14: E=60.3 MeV/nucleon beam of {+86}Kr from GANIL accelerator    
 61FE2c  using SISSI production target device coupled to the system of the      
 61FE3c  Alpha and LISE3 spectrometers. {+86}Kr with intensity of 15 pnA        
 61FE4c  impinged on a rotating natural Ni target 100 |mm thick.                
 61FE5c  Measured E|g, I|g and half-life using standard tof technique.          
 61FE c  2015Wi02: measured half-life of the 861, 9/2+ isomer using a new       
 61FE2c  technique of identifying nanosecond isomers produced in secondary      
 61FE3c  reactions with intermediate beam-energy radioactive ions beams at      
 61FE4c  NSCL-MSU facility using S-800 spectrograph for reaction products,      
 61FE5c  GRETINA array for prompt |g rays and CsI(Na) array for delayed         
 61FE6c  transitions. Measured {+61}Fe ions)|g(t)                               
